WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.840
So I think, you know, we have a quite a broad effort to always think about this, but we don't

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.560
want to over-promise at this stage, sitting here in 2026, what may or may not happen five years

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.620
from now. But rest assured, those efforts are ongoing, and as soon as we have something that

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.260
we think is credible to put forward, we certainly will let the markets know.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:29.300
Thank you. Your next question today comes from the line of Naresh Chohan from Intron Health.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:35.480
Please go ahead. Hi there. Thanks for taking my question. Just one thing on carcinetics.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.840
As we think about the margin impact of the carcinetics LOE,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:46.040
is it fair to assume that you've already started optimizing the profitability of carcinetics

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:53.460
as would be typical ahead of any other LOE? Thank you. Thanks, Naresh. I'll give that to Mukul.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.720
Yeah, Naresh, thanks for the question. Yeah, absolutely, I would confirm that. I think,

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:05.940
as we have previously indicated, I think we've projected an LOE in the U.S. for carcinetics in

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.820
2029. There is also an IRA event in 2020. So, I think, you know, we're going to have to

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:15.520
think about that in 2028 that we have factored into our numbers, and this is all baked into our

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:23.940
back to 40% latest by 2029 guidance in the margin. Thank you. Perfect. Thanks, Mukul.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:32.700
Thank you. Your next question comes from the line of Seamus Fernandez from Guggenheim Securities.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:39.460
Please go ahead. This is Zach Dunn on behalf of Seamus Fernandez. Thank you for the questions.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.660
We're encouraged by...

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:49.620
the advancement of your IL-15, the GIA632 into vitiligo. Can you share your thoughts on how

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:55.120
you think about the market size of biologic eligible vitiligo patients? And if you don't

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:01.560
mind tying that into your thoughts on atopic dermatitis and the market opportunity there.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:08.300
Thank you. Yeah, thanks. I mean, the IL-15 is something we did mention at the meet the

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.460
management, and we are quite excited by...

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.080
the profile of the...

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:19.680
over, you know, of this medicine. You know, for those of you who are not aware, this is a medicine that we in-license.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:27.000
It's overexpressed in patients with atopic dermatitis, but we also see the opportunity to address a number of other,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:34.760
you know, diseases over time, including, including vitiligo. And so it's early days. I mean, these phase two studies are ongoing.

